WEBVTT

00:00:00.424 --> 00:00:02.723
Lolly was built in the middle of the

00:00:02.827 --> 00:00:05.653
biggest change in how media gets made

00:00:05.721 --> 00:00:08.674
since the printing press, by people who

00:00:08.748 --> 00:00:11.242
are neither panicked about AI nor

00:00:11.322 --> 00:00:13.319
breathless about it.

00:00:14.088 --> 00:00:16.680
This page states the project's position

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:19.677
plainly and pairs every claim with the

00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:23.084
mechanism that enforces it, so you can

00:00:23.145 --> 00:00:25.669
verify rather than trust.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.249
"We're drinking like the tap will run dry

00:00:29.321 --> 00:00:30.719
any moment.

00:00:31.474 --> 00:00:34.796
It won't - today's AI is the worst it will

00:00:34.864 --> 00:00:36.094
ever be.

00:00:36.852 --> 00:00:39.945
If we survive the flood, it won't be by

00:00:40.012 --> 00:00:42.389
hoarding what's in the rusty water tank

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:45.344
down the hill, full of sediment.

00:00:46.104 --> 00:00:48.847
It will be by irrigating and reclaiming

00:00:48.940 --> 00:00:52.269
our land for a prosperous future."

00:00:53.012 --> 00:00:56.296
- Andy Fitzsimon, Lolly Contributor

00:00:57.419 --> 00:01:00.643
To be precise about it, because this page

00:01:00.732 --> 00:01:03.953
argues that precision matters: the image

00:01:04.005 --> 00:01:07.394
above is generated, not photographed.

00:01:08.193 --> 00:01:11.149
No camera was pointed at that homestead,

00:01:11.209 --> 00:01:13.893
because there is no homestead.

00:01:14.648 --> 00:01:17.072
It describes regional Queensland,

00:01:17.144 --> 00:01:19.893
Australia, prompted from The United

00:01:19.955 --> 00:01:23.539
Kingdom, generated in a datacenter in the

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:25.369
United States.

00:01:26.114 --> 00:01:29.081
It attempts to be faithful to a place

00:01:29.148 --> 00:01:32.187
without being a record of one, and that

00:01:32.247 --> 00:01:34.913
distinction is the entire reason its

00:01:34.975 --> 00:01:37.520
Content Credentials say so.

00:01:38.308 --> 00:01:40.881
Here is what that looks like when you

00:01:40.956 --> 00:01:42.318
check it.

00:01:43.110 --> 00:01:46.144
Nine steps survive in the file: five

00:01:46.201 --> 00:01:49.184
recorded by Google as it generated and

00:01:49.264 --> 00:01:52.220
watermarked the image, then four recorded

00:01:52.279 --> 00:01:56.032
by Lolly as it opened, created, marked and

00:01:56.093 --> 00:01:59.020
converted the version on this page.

00:01:59.821 --> 00:02:02.909
Lolly did not generate anything, and its

00:02:02.975 --> 00:02:04.768
entry says so.

00:02:05.546 --> 00:02:08.906
Andy's metaphor for a flood is this: the

00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:11.768
scarcity posture toward AI - invest

00:02:11.857 --> 00:02:14.486
everything in the few, diminish yourself

00:02:14.547 --> 00:02:17.318
today and worry later - is drinking

00:02:17.412 --> 00:02:20.328
spoiled tank water while the rain sets in

00:02:20.391 --> 00:02:23.041
and floodwater races across the plains

00:02:23.102 --> 00:02:24.495
toward you.

00:02:25.273 --> 00:02:28.123
Generated content is about to be

00:02:28.178 --> 00:02:30.218
effectively infinite.

00:02:30.977 --> 00:02:33.730
When something becomes infinite, its value

00:02:33.790 --> 00:02:36.341
moves to whatever remains scarce around

00:02:36.407 --> 00:02:39.883
it: trust, provenance, brand coherence and

00:02:39.944 --> 00:02:41.570
human judgment.

00:02:42.382 --> 00:02:45.273
Lolly is not a bigger bucket for the

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:46.493
flood.

00:02:47.241 --> 00:02:49.826
It is irrigation - channels that direct

00:02:49.886 --> 00:02:52.981
the water, and soil where things actually

00:02:53.043 --> 00:02:54.120
grow.

00:02:55.252 --> 00:02:58.029
The stance, in five commitments

00:02:58.969 --> 00:03:02.038
AI is welcome as input, never as

00:03:02.098 --> 00:03:03.844
impersonation.

00:03:04.609 --> 00:03:07.618
Agents are first-class users of Lolly:

00:03:07.678 --> 00:03:10.306
they run the same tools people do, through

00:03:10.362 --> 00:03:14.278
the MCP server and URL mode, inside

00:03:14.337 --> 00:03:16.995
exactly the same constraints.

00:03:17.749 --> 00:03:20.794
A tool that cannot emit an off-brand asset

00:03:20.893 --> 00:03:24.275
for a person cannot emit one for an agent

00:03:24.336 --> 00:03:27.278
either - the guard-rails do not care who

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:29.345
is throwing the ball.

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:32.843
What no agent gets to do is pass its

00:03:32.927 --> 00:03:36.019
output off as something it is not.

00:03:36.805 --> 00:03:39.543
AI declares itself.

00:03:40.310 --> 00:03:43.673
When AI generated the pixels, the export

00:03:43.733 --> 00:03:46.858
says so: a machine-readable assertion in

00:03:46.903 --> 00:03:49.675
the file's Content Credentials and a

00:03:49.736 --> 00:03:53.052
visible GEN AI badge when anyone verifies

00:03:53.103 --> 00:03:53.995
it.

00:03:54.792 --> 00:03:58.006
Lolly also reads and surfaces the AI

00:03:58.067 --> 00:04:01.425
declarations of files made elsewhere, and

00:04:01.523 --> 00:04:04.870
flags when a SynthID watermark is likely

00:04:04.932 --> 00:04:07.903
present - reading the declaration, not the

00:04:07.985 --> 00:04:09.869
watermark itself.

00:04:10.642 --> 00:04:13.525
The same rule binds Lolly's own on-device

00:04:13.586 --> 00:04:16.808
rewriter: every sentence it writes carries

00:04:16.857 --> 00:04:19.659
a public statistical watermark in its word

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:23.497
choices, disclosed here and in the tool,

00:04:23.571 --> 00:04:26.683
so text a model wrote stays self-declaring

00:04:26.780 --> 00:04:30.273
even as a plain-text copy - and anyone can

00:04:30.334 --> 00:04:33.019
check it on the Verify page.

00:04:33.777 --> 00:04:36.223
The scheme is public by design:

00:04:36.285 --> 00:04:39.343
verification for everyone, secrets for no

00:04:39.404 --> 00:04:40.320
one.

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:43.986
Audiences deserve to know how media was

00:04:44.047 --> 00:04:46.704
made - that sentence appears on our

00:04:46.771 --> 00:04:49.727
Inclusive Design page as an ethical

00:04:49.788 --> 00:04:52.712
commitment, and this is what makes it

00:04:52.795 --> 00:04:53.869
real.

00:04:54.646 --> 00:04:56.974
And when media you have declared as

00:04:57.064 --> 00:05:00.526
AI-made is placed into a design, the

00:05:00.607 --> 00:05:04.033
export's own credential says so too: a

00:05:04.096 --> 00:05:06.996
composite origin mark and a signed,

00:05:07.054 --> 00:05:10.119
machine-readable AI disclosure.

00:05:10.870 --> 00:05:13.669
Provenance is default-on.

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.098
Exports carry Content Credentials by

00:05:17.153 --> 00:05:20.294
default, not as a buried setting.

00:05:21.062 --> 00:05:24.494
The chain covers edits and ingredients, so

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:27.469
a work's history travels with it.

00:05:28.253 --> 00:05:31.493
You can verify this yourself on any file

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.369
Lolly produces.

00:05:34.128 --> 00:05:36.868
People stay the authors.

00:05:37.635 --> 00:05:40.847
Every input is ultimately a decision,

00:05:40.918 --> 00:05:43.994
triggered somewhere by a person, no matter

00:05:44.072 --> 00:05:47.019
how many systems or left turns it took to

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.319
get here.

00:05:49.099 --> 00:05:53.394
An agent can carry a decision a long way.

00:05:54.156 --> 00:05:56.969
It cannot originate one.

00:05:57.748 --> 00:06:00.156
The words, the image, the palette, the

00:06:00.222 --> 00:06:03.140
call that needed judgment: tools scale

00:06:03.189 --> 00:06:06.369
that judgment, they do not replace it.

00:06:07.127 --> 00:06:10.368
The tedious parts are what get automated:

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.927
the brand-checking, the re-exporting at

00:06:13.009 --> 00:06:15.920
every size, the hand-localising.

00:06:16.709 --> 00:06:19.893
What remains is the authorship.

00:06:20.664 --> 00:06:23.018
Channels, not buckets.

00:06:23.787 --> 00:06:26.513
Today's models are the floor, not the

00:06:26.618 --> 00:06:29.778
ceiling, so we refuse to build anything

00:06:29.839 --> 00:06:32.474
whose value depends on hoarding access to

00:06:32.535 --> 00:06:33.520
them.

00:06:34.294 --> 00:06:37.756
The engine is open source, renders on your

00:06:37.818 --> 00:06:40.594
own device and works offline.

00:06:41.351 --> 00:06:44.719
There is no model moat, no usage meter, no

00:06:44.794 --> 00:06:47.218
scarcity business attached to the flood

00:06:47.256 --> 00:06:48.445
itself.

00:06:49.217 --> 00:06:51.398
The durable investment is the

00:06:51.489 --> 00:06:54.571
infrastructure around the water - and that

00:06:54.645 --> 00:06:57.844
infrastructure is what we give away.

00:06:58.975 --> 00:07:01.714
Human decision is the point

00:07:02.704 --> 00:07:05.753
Let us be crystal clear about what sits

00:07:05.834 --> 00:07:08.694
underneath every commitment above.

00:07:09.450 --> 00:07:12.057
Individuals shape the earth and our

00:07:12.119 --> 00:07:13.319
history.

00:07:14.094 --> 00:07:17.360
Their choices, made one at a time, become

00:07:17.422 --> 00:07:20.369
the world the rest of us live in.

00:07:21.152 --> 00:07:23.694
Their actions make it.

00:07:24.459 --> 00:07:27.435
That is not sentiment, it is simply how

00:07:27.533 --> 00:07:29.869
anything has ever happened.

00:07:30.663 --> 00:07:34.125
So we empower human decision and we do not

00:07:34.187 --> 00:07:35.894
compromise it.

00:07:36.686 --> 00:07:39.067
The right to choose.

00:07:39.854 --> 00:07:41.365
Agency.

00:07:42.163 --> 00:07:43.667
Autonomy.

00:07:44.438 --> 00:07:47.783
The ability to decide and to act, and for

00:07:47.827 --> 00:07:50.044
that act to be yours.

00:07:50.825 --> 00:07:54.893
Tools here scale what a person decided.

00:07:55.646 --> 00:07:58.420
They do not decide instead of them, and

00:07:58.450 --> 00:08:01.595
they never quietly stand in for them.

00:08:02.364 --> 00:08:05.767
Where a decision is carried by automation,

00:08:05.829 --> 00:08:08.631
the record still leads back to the person

00:08:08.685 --> 00:08:11.717
who triggered it, however many systems and

00:08:11.777 --> 00:08:14.945
left turns it passed through on the way.

00:08:15.717 --> 00:08:18.695
We honour that end to end, and we record

00:08:18.759 --> 00:08:21.930
it: for history, for accountability, for

00:08:22.001 --> 00:08:24.194
trust and for tomorrow.

00:08:25.315 --> 00:08:27.595
AI, on your terms

00:08:28.590 --> 00:08:31.568
You never need AI here.

00:08:32.332 --> 00:08:35.569
If you choose it, three things hold:

00:08:36.375 --> 00:08:38.968
You are in control.

00:08:39.730 --> 00:08:43.178
AI helps only when you ask, and only with

00:08:43.237 --> 00:08:45.495
the piece you point it at.

00:08:46.302 --> 00:08:49.543
Nothing is decided for you.

00:08:50.302 --> 00:08:52.469
It stops costing.

00:08:53.223 --> 00:08:55.940
If AI helps make something once, the

00:08:56.002 --> 00:08:57.944
result is yours.

00:08:58.726 --> 00:09:02.061
Using it again is free, however many times

00:09:02.123 --> 00:09:03.569
you need it.

00:09:04.332 --> 00:09:06.469
It stays honest.

00:09:07.231 --> 00:09:10.847
A piece made by AI says so, and what you

00:09:10.902 --> 00:09:13.306
make carries your name instead of

00:09:13.368 --> 00:09:15.894
pretending to be someone else.

00:09:16.657 --> 00:09:19.812
Even the built-in help works this way: Ask

00:09:19.873 --> 00:09:22.097
Lolly answers with the manual's own

00:09:22.195 --> 00:09:24.860
sentence and a link, never a made-up

00:09:24.921 --> 00:09:26.045
answer.

00:09:27.176 --> 00:09:29.087
What this is not

00:09:30.075 --> 00:09:31.918
Not a ban.

00:09:32.693 --> 00:09:36.272
Tools may use AI where it serves the work,

00:09:36.341 --> 00:09:39.235
and agents are a supported audience - see

00:09:39.327 --> 00:09:41.119
AI Agents.

00:09:41.931 --> 00:09:44.668
Not a purity claim.

00:09:45.461 --> 00:09:48.324
Lolly reads provenance broadly and writes

00:09:48.387 --> 00:09:52.032
it honestly; it does not pretend to detect

00:09:52.125 --> 00:09:55.444
every generated pixel on the internet.

00:09:56.252 --> 00:09:58.768
Not a moral panic.

00:09:59.552 --> 00:10:02.593
The flood is not the enemy.

00:10:03.370 --> 00:10:06.220
Unattributed water is.

00:10:07.360 --> 00:10:10.025
How to hold us to it

00:10:11.007 --> 00:10:13.413
Every commitment above is enforced in the

00:10:13.481 --> 00:10:17.653
open codebase, not in a policy PDF: the

00:10:17.726 --> 00:10:21.118
provenance path, the GEN AI labelling and

00:10:21.161 --> 00:10:23.828
the no-trackers guarantee all ship with

00:10:23.898 --> 00:10:27.120
tests, and the Verify It Yourself page

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:29.260
walks you through checking the claims

00:10:29.314 --> 00:10:31.569
against a real export.

00:10:32.317 --> 00:10:34.908
If you find a place where the code and

00:10:34.946 --> 00:10:38.719
this page disagree, the code is the bug.
